// RUN: %gopp build -target=linux/arm64 -crt-dir=%aarch64_sysroot/lib %S/Inputs/core-init-order/c.gopp %S/Inputs/core-init-order/b.gopp %S/Inputs/core-init-order/a.gopp -o %t.cba
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-golden.py --qemu %aarch64_sysroot %t.cba %S/golden/core-init-order-cba.out
// RUN: %gopp build -target=linux/arm64 -crt-dir=%aarch64_sysroot/lib %S/Inputs/core-init-order -o %t.dir
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-golden.py --qemu %aarch64_sysroot %t.dir %S/golden/core-init-order.out
// P04.04 (manager decision M5): the core run tests built for linux/arm64
// and run under QEMU, with the expected output of the amd64 run (Go's on
// arm64 where it differs: golden/NAME.arm64.out). The normal suite keeps
// arm64 runs for core-init, core-option, core-fma, one differential table
// (diff-arm64.test) and the panic smoke test (core-panics-arm64.test).
